head_commit.message:
[XLA:CPU] Use index-permutation sorting for multi-input sorts and raw-pointer sorting for 1-input comparator sorts.

Multi-input CPU sorts (`num_inputs >= 3`, or `num_inputs == 2` with strided long slices or 16-byte elements) previously instantiated `std::sort` and `std::stable_sort` over a multi-buffer proxy iterator for arities 1 through 16 plus a dynamic-arity fallback, copying or swapping across all input buffers with per-input element-size switch dispatch on every O(N log N) comparison move/swap (and heap-allocating a temporary `std::vector` per move when `num_inputs > 16`). Instead, sort a contiguous array of slice indices `0..N-1` while keeping all input buffers read-only during the O(N log N) sort, and then permute each input buffer once in a single linear O(N) pass dispatched by element byte width (1, 2, 4, 8, 16 bytes) via `std::byte`-backed `ByteStorage<kBytes>`.

For single-input comparator sorts (`num_inputs == 1`) and strided 1D slices (`inner_dim_size > 1`), dispatch once by element byte width (1, 2, 4, 8, 16 bytes) and sort contiguous `ByteStorage<kBytes>` pointers directly (gathering/scattering strided slices through a contiguous buffer when `inner_dim_size > 1`), removing the custom multi-buffer `SortIterator` hierarchy (`~400` net lines removed).

Before vs. After:
```
// Before: 16 arity-specialized std::sort / std::stable_sort instantiations
// moving all k input buffers on every O(N log N) element move/swap:
SortIterator<Value<k>, Ref<k>, Ptr<k>> begin(Ptr<k>(&inputs), stride);
std::sort(begin, begin + n, compare);

// After (multi-input): 1 index sort + 1 linear O(N) permutation pass per input:
std::sort(indices, indices + n, compare_by_index);
for (size_t k = 0; k < num_inputs; ++k) {
  DispatchByElementSize(primitive_sizes[k], [&](auto elem) {
    PermuteSlice<decltype(elem)>(slice_base[k], stride, indices, scratch);
  });
}
```

Runtime and memory impact: Speeds up 1-input comparator sorts (`BM_Sort1D` with `LessThan` callback) by 1.24x-1.84x and multi-input sorts (`num_inputs = 8` and `25` with distinct buffers per input) by 1.05x-1.91x, while eliminating per-move heap allocations when `num_inputs > 16` and shrinking `sort_lib.pic.o` by 829.9 KB (-58.4%).

